# S13: Multi-Agent Task Handoff

## Objective

A single task can have a `lead_role` (primary owner) **plus** `helper_roles` (supporting agents).
The lead agent runs first, then optionally hands off steps to helpers. All agents appear in
board presence during their turn (S12). Enables ARCHITECT → QA → DEVOPS pipeline on a single task.

## Prerequisites

- S12 CLOSED (agent presence visible)
- `wc_tasks.lead_role` exists; `agent.activity` WS events work

## Tasks

- [x] S13-T01-FreezeInvariants.pd
- [x] S13-T02-SchemaHelperRoles.pd
- [x] S13-T03-HandoffStateMachine.pd
- [x] S13-T04-HandoffUiTask.pd
- [x] S13-T05-AgentConversation.pd
- [x] S13-T06-KnowledgeUpdate.pd
- [x] S13-T07-TestsSmoke.pd

## Definition of Done

- [x] Task with ARCHITECT lead + QA helper shows both agents running sequentially
- [x] Board activity timeline shows handoff events (agent.activity per actor)
- [x] Presence shows active agent during their turn
- [x] `bun run test` green — 344 passed (handoff.test.ts 2/2)

## App-agent protocol

All tasks follow `APP-AGENT-PROTOCOL.md`. Code tasks use `templates/PD-APP-AGENT-BLOCK.md`.

